Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 17:20:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09471/11362] [outer-loop] Preserve in-flight state before
 restarting the conductor

Commit-first before a restart: the conductor commits on its own cadence, and a
dirty tree at stop time is how transient work gets mixed into an unrelated
automated commit -- or lost, as happened twice today to concurrent edits.

Restarting to load the four self-improvement mechanisms committed this session
(truthful archival, guard-stall recovery, run receipts, verdict-class checks).
They live in scripts/research_conductor.py, which is a long-lived process, so
they were dormant until now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
